  "referee_audit_notes": [
    "REF1_SAKHAROV_NCHIRAL_50_NOTE: Producer's N=1 SUSY SO(10)->G_SMxU(1)_X a_1=(37/2 at xi=0, -7/2 at xi=1/6) uniquely corresponds to (N_v0=13, N_vp=32, N_chiral=50, i.e. 49 MSSM + 1 singlet S or 48 + 2). Full 3x16 + H_u(2) + H_d(2) has N_chiral=52 -> (39/2, -19/6), and IR MSSM 3x15 + H_u(2) + H_d(2) has N_chiral=49 -> (18, -11/3); all three preserve exact massive vector cancellation a_1(xi=0)==0 and identical UV sign flip (+ attractive at xi=0, - repulsive at xi=1/6). B5 (3x27 + 4 = 85 chiral) evaluates to (+36, +7/3) on its own spectrum vs shared benchmark (37/2, -7/2), leaving all 5-branch gate booleans unchanged.",
    "REF3_GL4_B3560_TRUNCATION_NOTE: On B=3500, V_0=50, disjoint implicit GL4 (N=300 and N=600) agrees with producer to <5e-12 (N=300) / <5e-13 (N=600). On B=3560, V_0=100, step-halved GL4 (N=300->600 self-convergence 1.29e-10) converges to phi_end=4.226940013202, R_end=1.005826456336, differing from producer's un-refined N=600 trajectory by 1.86e-10 abs (4.40e-11 rel) on phi and 1.40e-10 abs (1.39e-10 rel) on R, while R_max_60 matches to <1e-13; this O(1e-10) offset is purely producer's N=600 RK4 discretization truncation."
